audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Why do firms exist at all, if markets work so well? Herbert Simon''s visitor from Mars, the one who saw firms as green areas and markets as red lines, points the way.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Point its telescope at Harbourtown. The boatyard is a big green patch, Mia''s bakery a small one, and red lines run between them and out to the mainland.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:19iqrq1'
    '|a||Inside the green there are only faint blue lines: who reports to whom. No prices in there at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:vys8yb'
    '|b||Simon bet its report home would speak of large green areas interconnected by red lines, not a web of red lines with a few green dots. Is it true?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:14cnrh8'
    '|a||One check: count the workers who are employees, working inside the green for someone else, rather than for themselves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ry8zbj'
    '|b||Across the whole world it''s just over half. In the poorest countries, about one worker in five.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7o52jl'
    '|a||Now guess Norway.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ddvwxb'
    '|a||Drag Norway''s bar to your guess: what share of its workers are employees?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1oqxo8v'
    '|a||Ninety-five percent. The United States, ninety-four; Germany, ninety-two. That counts people working for the state too, but most work in firms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So in a rich economy almost everyone is directed by a boss, not by a price. Why, if prices coordinate so well?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1i9sw7q'
    '|a||In the early 1930s a young British student, Ronald Coase, crossed to America to look for an answer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Yes, the same Coase who wrote about pollution rights and lighthouses. This is a different idea, and his first.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:chj04l'
    '|a||Lenin had said Russia could be run as one big factory, and Western economists called that impossible. Yet Ford and General Motors were run from the top, and ran well.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:pnwhr0'
    '|b||And inside them, Coase wrote, a worker who moves from department Y to department X doesn''t go because relative prices changed. He goes because he is ordered to.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:c7cm54'
    '|a||His answer, published in 1937: there is a cost of using the price mechanism.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mly9w8'
    '|b||Take the boatyard, building one boat. It could buy every task on the market: the planks, the engine fitting, the paint, the rigging.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kxstgx'
    '|a||Each deal means finding the right price, haggling, writing a contract, and checking the work.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:x1pctj'
    '|b||Say each deal costs fifty dollars of time and lawyers, illustrative numbers. Four deals, two hundred dollars, and the same again for the next boat.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1lu8nnz'
    '|a||Or the yard hires the four workers once, on one contract each, and tells them every morning what to do.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:12kqi9u'
    '|b||Many deals replaced by a few long contracts. Those deal costs are the transaction costs that also block bargains over pollution.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1w0oxbi'
    '|a||Coase borrowed an image from Dennis Robertson: firms are islands of conscious power in this ocean of unconscious co-operation.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:18onbnt'
    '|b||So an island forms wherever telling someone is cheaper than buying from them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1t3i58c'
    '|a||If giving orders saves so much, why not one giant firm? Coase asked it too: why is not all production carried on by one big firm?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Because orders get dearer as the firm grows. Each extra task is one more thing for the boss to oversee, and mistakes creep in.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1thyois'
    '|a||Economists call it diminishing returns to management. Against it stands the cost of buying a task on the market: flat, say sixty dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:hiz0s5'
    '|b||Taking a task inside pays as long as organising it costs less than buying it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1w498vt'
    '|a||So the yard grows until the two costs meet, here at six tasks. That is Coase''s rule for where the firm ends.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:hiv7xg'
    '|b||Coase also named something that moves it: the telephone, which makes organising at a distance cheaper.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:yumxzv'
    '|b||The telephone makes organising at a distance cheaper. What happens to the boatyard?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:vna70a'
    '|b||It grows: the organising line falls, so the crossing moves right.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||It grows. The organising line tips down, and the meeting point moves out to ten tasks.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Cheaper markets, smaller islands; cheaper organising, bigger ones. The firm''s edge is a cost comparison, not a law of nature.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Want the boundary in one line of algebra?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1dgh80r'
    '|b||Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1okbz2u'
    '|a||Organising the x-th task inside costs c times x. Buying it costs m.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So the yard takes a task inside while c times x is below m.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1944bz3'
    '|a||The edge is where they are equal: x star equals m over c.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:16oldfz'
    '|b||Sixty over ten is six tasks. With the telephone, sixty over six is ten.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1u89ere'
    '|a||So the firm''s edge sits where two costs meet. But is an order really so different from a purchase?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Armen Alchian and Harold Demsetz said no, in 1972. A firm, they wrote, has no power of fiat.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1oti4cy'
    '|b||The boss can fire you or sue you. You can fire your grocer just as easily, by shopping somewhere else.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:calic7'
    '|a||To them a firm is a bundle of contracts with a boss in the middle, there to watch a team whose separate efforts are hard to measure.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:17h3axk'
    '|b||Simon disagreed. Employees accept authority over tasks no contract could list in advance, and many come to identify with the firm.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ejrr80'
    '|a||And neither side says which costs decide where a firm stops. Why does a carmaker build some parts and buy others? That''s make or buy, a question of its own.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:7pmygn'
    '|b||How sure are we? That firms exist because using markets has costs: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:8kbdt6'
    '|a||Which costs matter most, and whether an order differs from a purchase: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:3xpg2'
    '|b||Coase grumbled in 1972 that his paper was much cited and little used; in 1991 it helped win him the Nobel prize.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1t5k7ui'
    '|b||Order or price? Sort each move into where it happens.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:8ui9v3'
    '|a||A newspaper stops employing photographers and buys each photo from freelancers through an app. What most likely fell?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The cost of using the market: the app made each deal cheap, so the paper buys instead of employing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A software firm doubles in size and its managers drown in meetings. By Coase''s logic, what should it do?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Buy more from outside: organising has grown dearer than the market, so the edge moves in.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||All those meetings steepen the organising line, so the edge moves in.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So why do firms exist if markets work so well? Because using a market isn''t free.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ktoqst'
    '|a||Where telling is cheaper than buying, the green islands grow. Where it isn''t, the red lines take over.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:uvmceb'
    '|a||Yes: ninety-five percent.':
